thag15.2:12.1 starts: Like a white lotus,
# superseded: thag15.2:12.2 starts: born & growing in the water,
# superseded: thag15.2:12.3 starts: but not smeared by the water
# superseded: thag15.2:12.4 starts: —fragrant, delightful—
thag15.2:15.1 starts: Conveying an instructive meaning,
thag15.2:15.2 starts: this image is taught by the observant.
thag15.2:15.3 starts: Great nāgas will recognize
thag15.2:15.4 starts: the nāga as taught by the nāga
thag16.1:8.1 starts: Having attained the supreme Rightness,
thag16.1:8.2 starts: unconcerned with all the world,
thag16.1:8.3 starts: as if released from a burning house,
thag16.1:8.4 starts: he doesn’t sorrow at death.
thag16.1:12.1 starts: For one who sees, as it actually is,
thag16.1:12.2 starts: the pure arising of phenomena,
thag16.1:12.3 starts: the pure seriality of fabrications,
thag16.1:12.4 starts: there’s no fear.
thag16.1:14.1 starts: Dissatisfied with this carcass,
thag16.1:14.2 starts: I’m unconcerned with becoming.
thag16.1:14.3 starts: This body will break up
thag16.1:14.4 starts: and there will not be another.
thag16.4:23.1 starts: seeing this peril, I was then dismayed—
thag16.4:23.2 starts: pierced (with dismay),
thag16.4:23.3 starts: then calmed
thag16.4:23.4 starts: on attaining the end of the effluents.
thag16.7:1.1 starts: Whatever the fine clothes I wore
thag16.7:1.2 starts: when astride the elephant’s neck,
thag16.7:1.3 starts: whatever the fine rice I ate,
thag16.7:1.4 starts: the pure meat sauce,
thag16.1:1.1 starts: The bandit chief:
thag16.1:1.2 starts: we have killed in the past,
thag16.1:1.3 starts: against their will
thag16.1:1.4 starts: have trembled & babbled
thag16.1:3.1 starts: Ven. Adhimutta:
thag16.1:3.2 starts: chieftain,
thag16.1:3.3 starts: In one whose fetters are ended,
thag16.1:3.4 starts: all fears are overcome.
thag16.1:4.1 starts: With the ending of [craving]
thag16.1:4.2 starts: when phenomena are seen
thag16.1:4.3 starts: then as in the laying down of a
thag16.1:4.4 starts: there’s no fear in death.
thag16.1:13.1 starts: When seeing the world,
thag16.1:13.2 starts: as on a par
thag16.1:13.3 starts: finding no ‘mine-ness,’
thag16.1:13.4 starts: thinking, ‘There’s nothing of mine,’
thag16.1:15.1 starts: Do as you like with this carcass.
thag16.1:15.3 starts: From that I will feel
thag16.1:15.4 starts: neither hatred nor love.”
thag16.4:5.1 starts: Like a newly painted unguent pot—
thag16.4:5.2 starts: a putrid body adorned:
thag16.4:5.3 starts: enough to deceive a fool,
thag16.4:5.4 starts: but not a seeker for the further shore.
thag16.4:12.1 starts: So he burns, poked with sticks,
thag16.4:12.2 starts: in just one piece of cloth,
thag16.4:12.3 starts: They are not shelters for one who has
thag16.4:12.4 starts: not relatives,
thag16.4:16.1 starts: Thus the discernment by which
thag16.4:16.2 starts: is better than wealth—
thag16.4:16.3 starts: for those who haven’t reached mastery
thag16.4:16.4 starts: go from existence to existence,
thag16.4:25.1 starts: And the goal for which I went forth
thag16.4:25.2 starts: from home life into homelessness
thag16.4:25.3 starts: I’ve reached:
thag16.4:25.4 starts: the end
